IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth) -- the definitions the in-scope text uses
-- (section 3 terms used by ss 4AA to 4N) and section 4A.
--
-- A rule here answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE where the text gives the
-- meaning, JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words (a "means"
-- definition, "unless the contrary intention appears"), NOTHING where the
-- text lists without closing the list ("includes") or does not speak.
-- Every fork taken is numbered in NOTES.md.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 (Cth) s 3 terms used by ss 4AA-4N, and s 4A`

§§ `Section 3(1): State and Territory`

-- The opening words of section 3(1) are "In this Act, unless the contrary intention
-- appears:" and governs every definition in it, so each of the four rules below
-- takes the yes/no input `a contrary intention appears`. Where it is yes, the
-- definition does not apply: a rule that states what a term includes or means
-- answers JUST FALSE; the rule for Territory, which states what the term does
-- not include, answers NOTHING, because the text then says nothing about it.
-- src:41 | (1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:
@ref s 3(1) opening words (src:41)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` IS
    IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Only one place is told apart, because the text says only one thing about
-- the places: that a State includes the Northern Territory and that a
-- Territory does not.
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    NorthernTerritory
    `any other place`

-- src:151 | State includes the Northern Territory.
@ref s 3(1) State (src:151)
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) a place is a State` IS
    IF `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` `a contrary intention appears` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the place`
         WHEN NorthernTerritory THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:163 | Territory does not include the Northern Territory.
@ref s 3(1) Territory (src:163)
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) a place is a Territory` IS
    IF `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` `a contrary intention appears` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the place`
         WHEN NorthernTerritory THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 3(1): quarter`

-- src:146 | quarter means a period of 3 months ending on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September or 31 December.
@ref s 3(1) quarter (src:146)
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the last day` IS A DATE
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) a period is a quarter` IS
    IF `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` `a contrary intention appears` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST (`the first day of the quarter ending on` `the last day` EQUALS JUST `the first day`)

§§ `Section 3(1): property`

DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    Money
    `a thing capable of being the subject of ownership`
    `something else`

-- src:144 | property includes money and every thing, animate or inanimate, capable of being the subject of ownership.
@ref s 3(1) property (src:144)
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) a thing is property` IS
    IF `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` `a contrary intention appears` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the thing`
         WHEN Money THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a thing capable of being the subject of ownership` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 3(1): child`

-- The entry says who is the child of a person for the purposes of the Act, and
-- it says "without limiting", so it does not close the list. Sections 4M and 4N
-- take a child's age as an input and do not use this entry (NOTES.md, fork F26).
-- src:52 | child: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes of this Act, someone is the child of a person if he or she is a child of the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975.
@ref s 3(1) child (src:52)
GIVEN `he or she is a child of the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) someone is the child of a person` IS
    IF `s 3(1) the definitions in this subsection apply` `a contrary intention appears` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `he or she is a child of the person within the meaning of the Family Law Act 1975` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 3(2): fine`

DECLARE FineKind IS ONE OF
    `a pecuniary penalty of a kind not listed in s 3(2)(a)`
    `a pecuniary penalty imposed under Division 3 of Part XIII of the Customs Act 1901`
    `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a pecuniary penalty order, a literary proceeds order or an unexplained wealth order made under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
    `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a pecuniary penalty order made under the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987`
    `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a superannuation order made under the Australian Federal Police Act 1979`
    `a pecuniary penalty imposed by a superannuation order made under the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989`
    `costs or other amounts ordered to be paid by offenders`
    `something else`

-- src:189 | (2) In this Act, a reference to a fine includes a reference:
-- src:190 | (a) to a pecuniary penalty other than a pecuniary penalty imposed:
-- src:191 | (i) under Division 3 of Part XIII of the Customs Act 1901; or
-- src:192 | (ii) by a pecuniary penalty order, a literary proceeds order or an unexplained wealth order made under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002; or
-- src:193 | (iia) by a pecuniary penalty order made under the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987; or
-- src:194 | (iii) by a superannuation order made under the Australian Federal Police Act 1979; or
-- src:195 | (iv) by a superannuation order made under the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989; or
-- src:196 | (b) to costs or other amounts ordered to be paid by offenders.
@ref s 3(2) (src:189-196)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A FineKind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(2) a reference to a fine includes a reference to` IS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a pecuniary penalty of a kind not listed in s 3(2)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `costs or other amounts ordered to be paid by offenders` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4A: committed for trial and indictment`

DECLARE Committal IS ONE OF
    `committed to prison with a view to the person being tried before a judge and jury`
    `admitted to bail upon a recognizance to appear and be so tried`
    `dealt with in some other way`

-- src:4333 | In a law of the Commonwealth, unless the contrary intention appears:
-- src:4334 | committed for trial, in relation to a person, means committed to prison with a view to the person being tried before a judge and jury, or admitted to bail upon a recognizance to appear and be so tried.
@ref s 4A committed for trial (src:4333-4334)
GIVEN `how the person was dealt with` IS A Committal
      `the term is used in a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4A a person is committed for trial` IS
    IF NOT `the term is used in a law of the Commonwealth`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `how the person was dealt with`
              WHEN `dealt with in some other way` THEN JUST FALSE
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE ChargingDocument IS ONE OF
    Indictment
    Information
    Presentment
    `another document`

-- src:4333 | In a law of the Commonwealth, unless the contrary intention appears:
-- src:4334 | committed for trial, in relation to a person, means committed to prison with a view to the person being tried before a judge and jury, or admitted to bail upon a recognizance to appear and be so tried.
-- src:4335 | indictment includes an information and a presentment.
@ref s 4A indictment (src:4333-4335)
GIVEN `the document` IS A ChargingDocument
      `the term is used in a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4A a document is an indictment` IS
    IF NOT `the term is used in a law of the Commonwealth`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the document`
              WHEN `another document` THEN NOTHING
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
